@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-loads-under-node
`@pulls.review/core` MUST load under plain Node: no Settings, vue-i18n, `localStorage`,
`document` or Vite-only syntax inside it. Callers pass model settings and locale in
(architecture, Layout).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] engine-brief-is-openui-data
A brief or tour page is written in OpenUI Lang against the component library in
`brief.ts`; components take references (a changed path and line), never retyped data, and
an unknown component never renders. Only the Lang is stored; clients get a plain tree,
never the Lang, and output is data, never executed (architecture, The brief).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-tours-vary-their-form
The tour instructions ask the model to use the OpenUI components so each stop takes the
form that reads best (a flow, a table, a tree, code, a callout), not the same paragraphs
every time ("it looks a bit boring to read", recording 15 Oct 13:54, 07:46 to 08:14;
K17).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-mentions-are-links
An analysis run for the app writes every place it names as a repository-relative
Markdown link (`MENTION_RULE`), which clients turn into a jump to that line (rule 96;
architecture, Sharing).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-shapes-are-schemas
Canonical shapes (`DiffsPayload`, `GroupedResult`, `PrCacheEntry`, ...) are valibot
schemas first, validated where data is untrusted or versioned: a provider's raw answer
and an entry read back from storage (architecture, Canonical data structures).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-files-keyed-by-sha
Every `FileChange` carries a `sha` (GitHub's blob SHA, else one read from the patch's
`index` line, else a SHA-256 of the patch), and persisted review state is keyed by it
(architecture, Canonical data structures).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-chat-history-survives-writes
A diff's earlier chats (`LlmSession.archive`) are part of the stored session schema, so
they are read back from storage, and a `setLlmSession` write that leaves `archive` out
MUST keep the stored one: a chat turn, a new analysis or the page writing its transcript
never drops the chat history. Only an explicit `archive` (an empty list included) or
clearing the whole session replaces it (recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L36).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-tour-previews-while-it-builds
While a tour builds, `runTour` MUST put the plan's outline on its done `tour-plan` entry
as JSON (`{ title, overview, stops: [{ title, purpose }] }`), and each stop it writes on a
done `tour-stop:<index>` entry titled `Wrote <stop title>` whose `text` is that `TourStop`
as JSON, exactly as the result holds it. A failed stop adds no such entry, and the
previews MUST NOT change the result (recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L26).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-sources-say-what-a-place-does
A tour stop's source `why` is asked for as one short, plain sentence a reader new to the
code understands, saying what that place does for the stop, under about 90 characters,
with no jargon fragments and no name the path already shows. Captions such as "cleanup
trap" or "fifo opened read-write on fd 3" are what this prevents ("what does that mean?",
recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L29).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-excerpts-name-their-language
The tour and chat instructions MUST ask for code excerpts fenced with the real language of
their file and never `text`, and `splitTourBody` MUST give an excerpt fenced as `text`,
`txt`, `plain`, `plaintext` or nothing an empty language, so no block is labelled "Code
text" ("why does it say code, and why does it say text?", recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37,
L30).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-pseudocode-stays-short
Pseudocode is asked for as at most about 12 short lines, each under about 50 characters,
indented two spaces per level, in plain words over symbols and one idea per block;
anything longer becomes a list or prose ("pseudocode looks ugly as sin", recording 15 Oct
2026 15:37, L27).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-answers-draw-like-tours
The chat instructions MUST offer answers the same native forms a tour stop has, with the
same fence syntax word for word (`NATIVE_FORMS`), prose first and at most two visuals in
one answer ("so it can build interfaces that are as clean as it wants right here too to
reply to me", recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L34).
